  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1215 PM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nThe omega block pattern remains through the end of the week \nbefore eventually showing signs of breaking down as a decent \ntrough tries to dislodge it over the southwestern CONUS. As this \nhappens we should have a few more days of warm and dry weather \n(highs in the 80s lows in the 50s) before we get into low chances \nfor precip as moisture and humidity return on the back of \nsoutheasterly flow. This should allow temperatures to cool \nslightly as this trough begins to eject northeastward into the \npanhandles and thus possibly bringing with it a front southward \ninto our area. Long range models are still having quite a \ndifficult time handling this feature and the ensuing pattern \nchange. For now have kept pops low, in the 15-30% range, starting\nSunday and continuing into early next week. Continue to stay \ntuned as details become more refined as we get closer to the \nweekend.",
